---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const updated = '13 September 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${SITE.name} handles data: what stays in your browser, what cookies advertising partners may set, and your choices.`}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      Text you paste into any tool on {SITE.name} is processed by JavaScript running in your own browser. It is not transmitted
      to us or to anyone else. The only data collection on this site comes from standard web-server logs and from the
      advertising and analytics partners described below.
    </p>

    <h2>Data you enter into tools</h2>
    <p>
      Our tools are static web pages. When you paste a list, the conversion happens on your device and the result is displayed
      on the same page. We have no server component that receives, stores or inspects that content. Closing the tab discards it.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      Like virtually every website, our hosting provider records basic request information — IP address, browser type, the
      page requested and the time — for security and capacity planning. These logs are retained for a limited period and are
      not combined with any other data.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google AdSense to display advertisements. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to serve
      ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites. You can opt out of personalised advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Ads Settings</a>, and learn more about how
      Google uses data from sites that use its services at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener nofollow">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland will be shown a consent message before any
      personalised advertising cookies are set, and can change their choice at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use Google Analytics 4 to see which tools are used and how often: page views, which tool page was opened, whether a
      conversion succeeded or failed (as a category such as “invalid JSON”, never the text itself), which options and buttons
      were pressed (copy, download, clear), the rough size of the input (a bucket such as “under 1,000 characters”), and
      which internal links were followed. What you type or paste into a tool is never sent — the analytics code is
      written so that it cannot carry that text, and a test in the codebase enforces it. Analytics runs only on the
      published site, not while the site is being developed. Google Analytics 4 does not log or store IP addresses. The reports we see are
      aggregated and cannot identify you. You can prevent collection with the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener nofollow">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>
      or any content blocker; the tools work identically either way.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} itself sets no cookies. It uses your browser's local storage for exactly two things: the light/dark
      theme you pick with the toggle in the header, and, when you press a "Split back to column" or "Join into a list"
      button, the text being handed to the other tool for the length of that page change. Both stay on your device and
      are never sent anywhere. Third-party cookies may be set by the advertising and analytics services above. Most
      browsers let you block or delete cookies in their settings; the tools on this site continue to work with cookies
      disabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We will update this page if our practices change and revise the date at the top. Continued use of the site after a change constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      This site is operated by {SITE.author} (see <a href="/about">About</a>). Questions about privacy can be raised on the
      {' '}<a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
